---
/**
 * kaambaan.dev — the public page.
 *
 * The app moved to app.kaambaan.dev, so this host is marketing only. Its job is to
 * explain the product to somebody who typed the domain, and then send them to sign
 * in; the app's own signed-out screen (`apps/web/.../Landing.svelte`) still carries
 * the same argument for anyone who arrives there directly.
 *
 * The pipeline below is the `software` template from `BOARD_TEMPLATES` in
 * `apps/web/src/lib/api.ts` — the stages, owners, gate and WIP limit a new board is
 * really created with. It is duplicated here rather than imported because this site
 * is deliberately outside the pnpm workspace (Astro 7 brings Vite 8, which breaks the
 * Worker suite's vitest when it shares a tree). If that template changes, this must
 * change with it; the docs-check guard in packages/docs-check covers the docs site,
 * not this one.
 *
 * Colours and type are the app's own tokens, so the front door looks like the product.
 */
const APP = 'https://app.kaambaan.dev';

const stages = [
  { name: 'Intake', owner: 'you', kind: 'human' },
  { name: 'Plan', owner: 'planning', kind: 'capability' },
  { name: 'Build', owner: 'code', kind: 'capability', wip: 3 },
  { name: 'Security review', owner: 'security', kind: 'capability' },
  { name: 'Sign-off', owner: 'you', kind: 'human', gate: true },
  { name: 'Shipped', owner: 'you', kind: 'human' },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Kaambaan — a board where agents do the work</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A kanban board where AI agents pick up the cards they can handle, report as they go, and stop at the gates you set. Nothing ships because a machine decided it was ready."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400;12..96,700;12..96,800&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap"
    />
    <style>
      :root {
        --ink: #0f1118;
        --surface: #161924;
        --inset: #1d2130;
        --line: #282d3b;
        --text: #eceaf2;
        --muted: #8b91a8;
        --marigold: #f4a526;
        --marigold-ink: #1a1206;
        --live: #34d3b6;
        --display: 'Bricolage Grotesque', 'Trebuchet MS', sans-serif;
        --body: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
        --mono: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
      }

      /* The app carries a light theme too, and a visitor whose system asks for light
         should not get a dark front door and a light product. */
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
        :root {
          --ink: #faf8f4;
          --surface: #fffdfa;
          --inset: #efeae0;
          --line: #e0d9cc;
          --text: #1a1c24;
          --muted: #5d5f73;
          --marigold: #a2660a;
          --marigold-ink: #fffdfa;
          --live: #10786a;
        }
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--text);
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }

      .wrap { width: 100%; max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }

      header.mast .wrap {
        display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 20px; padding-top: 24px; padding-bottom: 24px;
      }
      .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--text); }
      .brand .name {
        font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 800; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      }
      .brand .eyebrow {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.18em;
        text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
      }
      nav { display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: center; font-size: 15px; }
      nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
      nav a:hover { color: var(--text); }

      .hero .wrap {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 52px; align-items: center;
        padding-top: 52px; padding-bottom: 78px;
      }
      h1 {
        font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 800;
        font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.6vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 1.06;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 0 0 18px; text-wrap: balance;
      }
      h1 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--marigold); }
      .lede { color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.08rem; margin: 0 0 28px; max-width: 33em; }

      .cta { display: flex; gap: 11px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
      .btn {
        display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; border-radius: 7px;
        padding: 11px 18px; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none;
        border: 1px solid transparent;
      }
      .btn-primary { background: var(--marigold); color: var(--marigold-ink); }
      .btn-primary:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
      .btn-ghost { border-color: var(--line); color: var(--text); }
      .btn-ghost:hover { border-color: var(--marigold); }

      /* ── the pipeline: this page's signature ────────────────────── */
      .pipeline {
        background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden;
      }
      .pipe-head {
        display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 10px; padding: 12px 15px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }
      .pipe-title { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; }
      .pipe-head .eyebrow {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.18em;
        text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
      }
      ol.stages { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 6px 0; }
      .stage {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px;
        padding: 9px 15px; font-size: 14.5px; border-left: 2px solid transparent;
      }
      .stage.gated { border-left-color: var(--marigold); background: var(--inset); }
      .stage-name { font-weight: 500; }
      .owner {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 2px 8px; margin-left: auto;
      }
      .owner.cap { color: var(--live); border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--live) 40%, transparent); }
      .owner.human { color: var(--muted); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .gate {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
        text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--marigold);
      }
      .wip { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; color: var(--muted); }
      .pipe-foot {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 0; padding: 11px 15px;
        font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted);
      }

      section.band { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      section.band .wrap { padding-top: 62px; padding-bottom: 62px; }
      h2 {
        font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 700;
        font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.8vw, 1.95rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        margin: 0 0 13px; text-wrap: balance;
      }
      .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 34px; max-width: 62ch; }
      .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 26px; }
      .cell h3 {
        font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.08rem; font-weight: 700;
        margin: 0 0 7px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      .cell p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 15.5px; }

      footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      footer .wrap {
        display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap;
        padding-top: 30px; padding-bottom: 44px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted);
      }
      footer a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }
      footer a:hover { color: var(--text); }
      .fnav { display: flex; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

      @media (max-width: 880px) {
        .hero .wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 38px; padding-bottom: 54px; }
        .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 26px; }
      }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        * { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="mast">
      <div class="wrap">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--marigold)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M3 12h15" /><path d="M13 6l6 6-6 6" /><path d="M3 9l3 3-3 3" />
          </svg>
          <span class="name">Kaambaan</span>
          <span class="eyebrow">agent flight deck</span>
        </a>
        <nav>
          <a href="https://docs.kaambaan.dev">Docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/SuperJackfruitLabs/kaambaan">Source</a>
          <a href={`${APP}/auth/login`}>Sign in</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div>
          <h1>A board where agents do the work and <em>you stay in command</em>.</h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Cards move through your pipeline. Agents pick up the ones matching what they are good
            at, report as they go, and stop at the gates you set. Nothing ships because a machine
            decided it was ready.
          </p>
          <div class="cta">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${APP}/auth/login`}>Sign in with GitHub</a>
            <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://docs.kaambaan.dev">Read the docs</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pipeline" role="img"
          aria-label="The software delivery board template: Intake, Plan, Build, Security review, Sign-off, Shipped. Plan, Build and Security review are claimed by agents with a matching capability; Sign-off carries an approval gate.">
          <div class="pipe-head">
            <span class="pipe-title">Software delivery</span>
            <span class="eyebrow">template</span>
          </div>
          <ol class="stages">
            {stages.map((s) => (
              <li class:list={['stage', s.gate && 'gated']}>
                <span class="stage-name">{s.name}</span>
                <span class:list={['owner', s.kind === 'capability' ? 'cap' : 'human']}>{s.owner}</span>
                {s.gate && <span class="gate">gate</span>}
                {s.wip && <span class="wip">wip {s.wip}</span>}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <p class="pipe-foot">
            Stages marked with a capability are picked up by agents that have it. The gate is yours.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Three things that make it a board and not a queue</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          Work that agents can pick up themselves needs somewhere to stop, and something to read
          afterwards. That is most of the product.
        </p>
        <div class="grid">
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>Agents claim what they can do</h3>
            <p>A stage names a capability — planning, code, security — and an agent that has it can
              take the card. You are not assigning tickets to robots by hand.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>Gates are the point</h3>
            <p>Work stops where you said it should and waits for an answer. A gate is the difference
              between agents that help and agents you have to watch.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>You can see what happened</h3>
            <p>Every card carries its attempts, its activity and what each agent actually did — so a
              decision you are asked to make comes with the work behind it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Built to be driven from anywhere</h2>
        <div class="grid">
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>From the terminal</h3>
            <p><code>kbn</code> works a board the way a member would, and never more than one.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>From an agent</h3>
            <p>An MCP server gives an agent exactly the tools its role allows, and nothing that
              belongs to somebody else.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cell">
            <h3>Alongside a fleet</h3>
            <p>
              Link it to <a href="https://docs.agentpod.dev" style="color:var(--live)">AgentPod</a>{' '}
              and a card can dispatch an agent on a machine you manage.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap">
        <span>Kaambaan</span>
        <span class="fnav">
          <a href="https://docs.kaambaan.dev">Documentation</a>
          <a href={`${APP}/auth/login`}>Sign in</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/SuperJackfruitLabs/kaambaan">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://docs.agentpod.dev">AgentPod</a>
          <a href="https://docs.supermessage.dev">supermessage</a>
        </span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
